From ac8739de016406c9b0274d3d9df6a05b7f62ed8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JeyKul <77121325+JeyKul@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 20:17:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 53/56] wifi: brcmfmac: BCM4389 (Galaxy S22 series)

PCIe 14e4:4441, firmware brcmfmac4389c1-pcie (Samsung's bcmdhd_sta.bin,
nvram.txt, bcmdhd_clm.blob). What it needed, mostly following
Broadcom's DHD:
- CA7 + SYSMEM: RAM base 0x200000; SYSMEM bank counts in DHD's layout
  (rev 9: 21 RAM banks after 8 ROM banks = 2.6 MB); in download state
  reset SYSMEM and leave the 802.11 cores alone; CA7 before CR4.
- RAM larger than the 4 MB BAR1 window: move the window (config 0x84)
  for every TCM access.
- multi-backplane: request the ARM/backplane power domain (DAR
  powerctl) before starting the firmware; the backplane is briefly
  unreachable while it boots (all ones): keep polling.
- 1535 rx buffers asked for: 2048 rx packet ids.
- random seed before NVRAM; deep sleep requests NAKed (no device-wake).
- join: the versioned wl_extjoin_params_v1 layout.
- firmware asserts sometimes without a FWHALT message: check the trap
  flag on each doorbell and reset the bus.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
